ine":"Power Rankings: The top teams hold their positions in Week 11","description":"Check out how Week 11 caused shifts in this week's top 25.","published":"2026-11-16T12:12:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50473507/2026-college-football-power-rankings-top-25-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079636/dom-nichols","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dominic_Nichols"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Dominic Nichols","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dominic_Nichols","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:11Z","intro":"Dominic Nichols (born February 6, 2006) is an American football defensive end for the Michigan Wolverines.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Nichols attended Oakdale High School in Frederick, Maryland. He was rated as a four-star recruit by 247Sports and committed to play college football for the Michigan Wolverines over offers from Clemson, Kentucky, and Wisconsin."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In the 2024 ReliaQuest Bowl, Nichols totaled two tackles and a forced fumble in an upset win over Alabama. As a freshman during the 2024 season, he played in five games, recording three tackles and a forced fumble. In 2025, Nichols notched 19 tackles with five and a half for a loss and a sack."}]}}